Shanling Q2 tools
=================

q2-subsonic runs from the card's .subsonic folder as a Q2 Pod card app (q2-pod's patch/addon.c): a
Subsonic (OpenSubsonic API) client that syncs and streams. Built from q2-filebrowser's scripts.

  build.sh     static Go for the Q2 and the card files, in target/shanlingq2/.subsonic, zipped as
               target/shanlingq2/q2-subsonic-vX.Y-SHA.zip (unzip that at the card's root)
  package.py   checks the binary (static, MIPS32 little-endian, soft-float ABI), sets the nan2008
               ELF flag the Q2's kernel requires and Go doesn't, and writes the ZIP
  launcher.sh  installed as .subsonic/run: q2-subsonic copied to /tmp and run there in a restart loop
  q2app        installed as .subsonic/q2app: the card app manifest (name=Subsonic, qr=0)
  icon.png, icon-40.png
               Streaming's row icon, 52 px (Legacy) and 40 px (iPod); placeholders
  test_launcher.py
               runs launcher.sh on the host with a fake app
